---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <section class="profile" aria-labelledby="profile-name">
      <div class="portrait" aria-label="Zeqing Wang initials">ZW</div>

      <div class="profile-copy">
        <h1 id="profile-name">Zeqing Wang</h1>
        <p>
          I am an M.S. student in Computer Science (Artificial Intelligence) at the
          University of Southern California. I received my bachelor's degree in Electronic
          and Computer Engineering from Shanghai Jiao Tong University.
        </p>
        <p>
          My research spans robot learning, world models, uncertainty quantification,
          3D vision and reconstruction, and human–robot interaction.
        </p>
        <p class="profile-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/Zing110" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/zeqing-wang-477405374/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}about/`}>About</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="interests-title">
      <h2 id="interests-title">Research Interests</h2>
      <div class="research-vision">
        <h3>Embodied Cognitive Agents</h3>
        <p class="vision-tagline">Robotic agents that know what to do, when to act, how to execute, and how to collaborate.</p>
        <p class="vision-statement">
          I aim to build integrated robotic agents that perceive the physical world, reason
          and plan with foundation models, retain and retrieve experience through persistent
          memory, execute through adaptive policies, and collaborate naturally with humans
          and other agents.
        </p>
        <div class="research-pillars">
          <p><strong>Perceive &amp; Ground</strong><span>Multimodal sensing, 3D vision, reconstruction, and grounded world models.</span></p>
          <p><strong>Reason &amp; Remember</strong><span>Foundation models, planning, uncertainty quantification, and persistent memory.</span></p>
          <p><strong>Plan &amp; Act</strong><span>Robot learning, vision-language-action policies, and adaptive control.</span></p>
          <p><strong>Interact &amp; Collaborate</strong><span>Human–robot interaction and coordination among multiple agents.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="news-title">
      <h2 id="news-title">News</h2>
      <ul class="news-list">
        <li><time datetime="2026-09">Sep 2026</time><span>Began research on uncertainty-aware policy evaluation with robotic world models at USC's SLURM Lab.</span></li>
        <li><time datetime="2025">2025</time><span>First-author paper on tracking-aware non-rigid 3D reconstruction published at IROS 2025.</span></li>
        <li><time datetime="2025">2025</time><span>Co-authored work on safe human–robot motion planning published in <em>Robotics and Computer-Integrated Manufacturing</em>.</span></li>
        <li><time datetime="2025-05">May 2025</time><span>Selected as a Shanghai Outstanding Graduate.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="research-title">
      <h2 id="research-title">Research</h2>
      <div class="research-list">
        <article class="research-item">
          <aside class="research-meta">
            <time>Sep 2026 – Present</time>
            <p>SLURM Lab, USC</p>
            <p>Advisors: Daniel Seita &amp; Yue Wang</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="research-body">
            <h3>Uncertainty Estimation for Policy Evaluation with Robotic World Models</h3>
            <p>Investigating when world-model rollouts can reliably replace costly real-robot policy evaluations.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Building a CTRL-World evaluation pipeline on the DROID Franka platform across in- and out-of-distribution tasks.</li>
              <li>Studying ensemble uncertainty, predictive disagreement, classifiers, and calibration for reliable policy ranking.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="research-item">
          <aside class="research-meta">
            <time>Dec 2025 – Apr 2026</time>
            <p>HaRVI Lab, USC</p>
            <p>Advisor: Heather Culbertson</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="research-body">
            <h3>Fast VR Scene Reconstruction and Haptic Mapping with 3D Gaussian Splatting</h3>
            <p>Designed an end-to-end workflow combining 3DGS reconstruction, semantic understanding, and haptic mapping to generate interactive VR environments in under one hour.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Developed automatic scene cropping and artifact removal to preserve relevant geometry.</li>
              <li>Integrated Splat Feature Solver to map semantic objects to vibrotactile effects.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="research-item">
          <aside class="research-meta">
            <a class="research-visual" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}tadf/`} aria-label="Open the TADF project page">
              <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/tadf-overview.gif`} alt="Input surgical video and the corresponding animated 3D deformation field" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            </a>
            <time>Mar 2024 – Feb 2025</time>
            <p>SIRIUS Lab, SJTU</p>
            <p>Advisor: Yutong Ban</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="research-body">
            <h3>Tracking-Aware Non-Rigid 3D Reconstruction for Robotic Surgery</h3>
            <p>Proposed TADF, incorporating CoTracker-based soft-tissue trajectories into a neural implicit reconstruction network.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Jointly reconstructed tissue geometry and deformation with a color-coded deformation-field visualization system.</li>
              <li>Reduced average deformation MSE from 0.322 to 0.288 and improved average PSNR from 30.978 to 32.043 dB.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="research-citation"><strong>Zeqing Wang</strong>, H. Fang, Y. Xu, and Y. Ban. “Tracking-Aware Deformation Field Estimation for Non-rigid 3D Reconstruction in Robotic Surgeries.” <em>IEEE/RSJ IROS</em>, 2025.</p>
            <p class="research-links"><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}tadf/`}>project page</a><span>/</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.02558" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">paper</a><span>/</span><a href="https://github.com/Zing110/TADF" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">code</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="research-item">
          <aside class="research-meta">
            <time>Oct 2023 – Jun 2024</time>
            <p>DDDIS Lab, SJTU</p>
            <p>Advisor: Youyi Bi</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="research-body">
            <h3>Towards safe motion planning for industrial human-robot interaction: A co-evolution approach based on human digital twin and mixed reality</h3>
            <p>Built a human digital-twin simulation in Unity and ML-Agents and trained A-IPPO for safe collaborative motion planning.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Validated collision detection and multi-stage reward design in simulated and physical collaboration tasks.</li>
              <li>Achieved 90.5–95.5% success with 3.1–6.3% collision rates and reduced collisions by 70.7% versus PPO on pick-and-place.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="research-citation">B. Feng, <strong>Zeqing Wang</strong>, L. Yuan, Q. Zhou, Y. Chen, and Y. Bi. “Towards safe motion planning for industrial human-robot interaction: A co-evolution approach based on human digital twin and mixed reality.” <em>Robotics and Computer-Integrated Manufacturing</em>, 95:103012, 2025.</p>
            <p class="research-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rcim.2025.103012" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">paper</a><span>/</span><a href="https://github.com/bohanfeng/Towards-Safe-Motion-Planning-for-Industrial-Human-Robot-Interaction" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">code</a><span>/</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iZl7r_tehIk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">video</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
      <h2 id="projects-title">Selected Projects</h2>
      <article class="project-item">
        <p class="project-meta">Course project · CSCI 544, USC · Sep–Dec 2025</p>
        <h3>Medical Question Answering via LoRA Fine-Tuning and Multi-Agent Collaboration</h3>
        <p>Fine-tuned Llama-3.1-8B and Qwen3-8B on MedMCQA and PubMedQA, then designed a Triage–Expert–Consultation framework for structured clinical reasoning.</p>
        <p><strong>Result:</strong> 79.03% accuracy on MedMCQA and a BERTScore F1 of 0.8473 for explanation quality.</p>
      </article>
      <p class="archive-link"><a href="https://github.com/Zing110?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse additional projects on GitHub →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="education-title">
      <h2 id="education-title">Education</h2>
      <div class="education-list">
        <article><div><h3>University of Southern California</h3><p>M.S. in Computer Science (Artificial Intelligence)</p></div><time>2025 – 2027</time></article>
        <article><div><h3>Shanghai Jiao Tong University</h3><p>B.Eng. in Electronic and Computer Engineering</p></div><time>2021 – 2025</time></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section misc-grid" aria-label="Additional academic information">
      <div>
        <h2>Honors</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li><span>Shanghai Outstanding Graduate</span><time>2025</time></li>
          <li><span>Gold Award, SJTU Undergraduate Capstone Project</span><time>2024</time></li>
          <li><span>Wu Jiong–Sun Jie Sunshine Scholarship</span><time>2024</time></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Leadership</h2>
        <div class="leadership-entry">
          <h3>President &amp; Founder, JI XR Club</h3>
          <p class="project-meta">2023 – 2024</p>
          <p>Organized AR/VR development workshops and led club projects and technical initiatives in extended reality.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section toolkit" aria-labelledby="toolkit-title">
      <h2 id="toolkit-title">Technical Toolkit</h2>
      <p><strong>Languages:</strong> Python, C++, C#, MATLAB</p>
      <p><strong>Frameworks &amp; tools:</strong> PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, OpenCV, Unity, ML-Agents, Linux, Git/GitHub, 3D Gaussian Splatting</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
